lithos-metal v0.1.2 (46b2bc4): map the untied MLX head name language_model.lm_head.* to lm_head.*

Base: ~/Developer/mlsys/serving/lithos-metal at tag v0.1.2, commit 46b2bc4cda57826c072d94afe90a58633aaeb6d9.
Not applied. See lithos-metal/env.md section 4 in the benchmark repo.

Why: mlx_lm.convert stores the untied head of Qwen3.8-27B as language_model.lm_head.{weight,scales,biases}.
Both mlx-community/Qwen3.8-27B-8bit (815b83c0) and mlx-community/Qwen3.8-27B-4bit (10c35caa) do
(tie_word_embeddings false, 2180 tensors, same key set). mlx_rename only maps language_model.model.*,
so binding fails with KeyError "checkpoint has no tensor group for 'lm_head.weight'".

The fix edits mlx_rename in place instead of wrapping it: bind_checkpoint_formats runs mlx_adapt (the
MLX norm un-fold) only when model.checkpoint_rename is mlx_rename, and SafetensorsDir applies the same
function for binding, packing (pack_plan.py) and tools/pack_weights.py.

Apply, from the lithos-metal checkout (the install is not editable, so reinstall afterwards):
  git apply --check <this file> && git apply <this file>
  uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -e '.[serve]'
Revert:
  git apply -R <this file>, then reinstall the same way.

diff --git a/monolith/models/qwen3_5/weights.py b/monolith/models/qwen3_5/weights.py
